Z||000000||drednot||06-07-2001||09:33 PM||||Check it--<P><BR> <A HREF="http://earlscheib.com/f-technology.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://earlscheib.com/f-technology.htm</A> <P><BR>and it won't cost more than a Fiero is worth!||||reg||10
Z||000001||Oreif||06-07-2001||09:48 PM||||Yes they paint any car any color. I know someone who had their car painted at one. They painted EVERYTHING. Headlights,Parking lights, dash board, seats, tires,etc they had so much over spray it wasn't funny. You get what you pay for.<P>BTW ~ 6 months later the paint started flaking off the trunk lid.||||reg||13
Z||000002||Shiner||06-07-2001||10:48 PM||||It's true.  If you painted the car yourself, just the paint cost would be more than they charge, and they include labor.  If it seems too good to be true......<P>------------------<BR>-Shiner-<BR>'84 Sport Coupe<BR>'87 GT<BR>'86 SE 2M6 (parts car)||||reg||1
Z||000003||maryjane||06-07-2001||11:00 PM||||Years ago I remeber Earl Sheib's TV commercials claiming" we will paint ANY car for $19.95!" Same quality then as now.<BR>Don||||reg||12
Z||000004||DecadenceR||06-08-2001||09:40 AM||||That's like Maaco paint.<BR>Great if you're selling the car in a week.<BR>Not something i'd want for a keeper.||||reg||1
Z||000005||stsmithgt||06-08-2001||09:43 AM||||They still give that bonus paint job of painting your tires, wheels, bumper, and windows at no EXTRA CHARGE? LOL<BR>Back in 1978 this girl at school had a Cuda they almost ruined.  It was ALL OVER puke green.<BR>You'd think they'd learn.  I suppose it depends on the shop too.||||reg||1
Z||000006||ThatRickGuy||06-08-2001||09:46 AM||||I don't know if Earl Sheib is the same as Maaco. Maacos are independently owened, and some of them provide really good paint jobs, although others leave you with crap. If you do use one of these companies, do all the sanding and prep work yourself, mask off anything you can.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Formula88||06-08-2001||10:10 AM||||I had my '69 Firebird painted by Earl Scheib back in High School.  Cost me $99.95 at the time.  The job turned out pretty good, but I did all the prep work myself and just dropped it off to be sprayed.  That was 18 years ago.  I found this car in a guy's front yard a couple of years ago and it still had the same paint job!  But, buy now it had faded to a powdery pink and would rub off on your hands.  Also, the tape pinstripes I put on were falling off because they were pulling the paint off!  Their paint is crap.  Their workmanship is crap.  They can't afford to be better.  If they had better skilled people and better equipment, they'd be working somewhere they could make more money.  That was my first car, and I almost bought it back.  Too bad someone had driven it offroad and ran over a stump.  Literally ripped the rear end out from under the car.  The guy said it was fixed, but who knows what kind of damage was done to the subframe/unibody?  Poor car.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  I had a LOT of good times in that baby!||||reg||1
Z||000008||DecadenceR||06-08-2001||10:17 AM||||Rick, that is true.<BR>But I'm talking about the Maaco's I've seen.<BR>My friend had a Monte Carlo SS painted silver by them.<BR>And they sprayed all his chrome, his headlights, his wipers... Plus there were a lot of runs in the paint.<BR>Then again, for $200, you do get what you pay for.||||reg||1
Z||000009||EdsB52||06-08-2001||11:38 AM||||I prepped and masked a 78 Ramchero years ago, took it in and had them paint it for $100. Worked out well. I think the paint last about 2 years for full quality, then slowly dropped off. But I was satisfied. I would never have them do everything. With Macco, it sems you delegate to them what kind of quality you want. If you pay $200, you get Scheib. If you pay 7-800, you get a pretty descent job, there's no free lunch.||||reg||1
Z||000010||84Bill||06-08-2001||11:45 AM||||Never ever take your car to MACCO I worked for the for 2 weeks and quit because I could not bring myself to rip people off by doing crappy work! Their Idea of sanding a car was to do 1 pass with 220 (DRY) and send it to the spray booth! didnt even take the shine off (finish should be completely hazy) or clean up the car prior to color.<BR>Really bad work ethic!||||reg||8
Z||000011||hyhy4u||06-08-2001||02:11 PM||||Earl Schieb paint is like...buying a ford, dont do it unless you wanna be back at the place 2 years from now with it all falling apart and looking like crap.||||reg||13
